+// Dialog callbacks and the retained dialog, exception and stream receipts belong
+// to the tab, not the renderer's lifecycle. During a navigation (a failed one, or
+// a renderer replacement) the attached primary frame can already be inactive
+// while its replacement is committing. Browser-owned control and receipts must
+// remain available in that interval without running or observing the old
